{"name":"Jimbaran Bay","hex":"#3d5d64","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jimbaran","blocks":[{"text":"Jimbaran is an Indonesian fishing village and tourist resort in southern Bali, administered under South Kuta District of Badung Regency. Located south of Ngurah Rai International Airport at the \"neck\" of the Bukit Peninsula, the village is renowned as a culinary destination, with stalls selling seafood saturating the area. Diners select the live seafood that they wish to eat, and it is immediately prepared, generally grilled over a fire of coconut husks rather than charcoal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Jimbaran200507-1.jpg/330px-Jimbaran200507-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimbaran","wikidata":"Q670243"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Jimabaran_beach.jpg/120px-Jimabaran_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Jimabaran_beach.jpg/250px-Jimabaran_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Jimabaran_beach.jpg/120px-Jimabaran_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJimabaran_beach.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Morning_catch_of_marlin_at_Jimbaran.jpg/120px-Morning_catch_of_marlin_at_Jimbaran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Morning_catch_of_marlin_at_Jimbaran.jpg/250px-Morning_catch_of_marlin_at_Jimbaran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Morning_catch_of_marlin_at_Jimbaran.jpg/120px-Morning_catch_of_marlin_at_Jimbaran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMorning_catch_of_marlin_at_Jimbaran.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/